# jansson -- JSON for NetworkManager.
#
# NetworkManager's meson takes it as
#     dependency('jansson', version: '>= 2.7', required: false)
# so this is an OPTIONAL dependency of NM and packaging it is a decision rather
# than a necessity. What it buys, and why it is worth a recipe:
#
# WHAT IT ENABLES. config_h.set10('WITH_JANSSON', ...) turns on NM's JSON
# handling, which is what parses and validates the JSON blobs in a connection
# profile -- team configurations, and the ovs external-ids. Without it NM
# builds, runs, and rejects any profile carrying one, with an error about JSON
# support rather than about the profile.
#
# THE SHARPER REASON, and it is a build-time one. NM does not link jansson; it
# dlopens it by SONAME at runtime. So its meson.build runs
#     readelf -d $(pkg-config --variable=libdir jansson)/libjansson.so
# at configure time, parses the SONAME out, and asserts 'Unable to determine
# Jansson SONAME' if it cannot (meson.build lines 268-284). That makes the
# UNVERSIONED development symlink a build input rather than a developer
# convenience, which is unusual enough to be worth writing down, and it is what
# post-install.sh asserts.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env -- versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/akheron/jansson/releases/download/v2.14.1/jansson-2.14.1.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=6bd82d3043dadbcd58daaf903d974891128d22aab7dada5d399cb39094af49ce
SRC_DIR=jansson-2.14.1

# --disable-static and nothing else. jansson's configure offers six options
# (configure.ac): --enable-urandom and --enable-dtoa default to yes and are the
# behaviour every distribution ships; --enable-windows-cryptoapi is Windows;
# --enable-initial-hashtable-order is a tuning constant; --enable-Bsymbolic is
# a linker experiment; --enable-ossfuzzers builds fuzz targets. None is a
# dependency probe, so unlike most recipes here there is no list of things that
# resolve off today for a reason that could change tomorrow.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static"
